From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:45:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] linux-dmabuf: advertise scan-out-only modifiers to
 version 3 clients

Clients that bind zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 below version 4 (e.g. GStreamer
1.26 waylandsink) only get the renderer's format/modifier pairs, so they
never use a scan-out-only pair such as the Allwinner video engine's
NV12 + DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ALLWINNER_TILED, although such buffers are now
accepted and put on a plane.

Also send the scan-out-only pairs of the feedback format table as
modifier events.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 libweston/linux-dmabuf.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libweston/linux-dmabuf.c b/libweston/linux-dmabuf.c
index 9b358ab..89a975c 100644
--- a/libweston/linux-dmabuf.c
+++ b/libweston/linux-dmabuf.c
@@ -1121,6 +1121,26 @@ bind_linux_dmabuf(struct wl_client *client,
 			}
 		}
 	}
+
+	/* Scan-out-only pairs (appended to the feedback format table after
+	 * the renderer's ones, see format_table_append()): a v3 client cannot
+	 * get the scanout tranche, so advertise them here. Only a client that
+	 * produces such buffers (e.g. a video decoder) will use them; they are
+	 * accepted as direct-display buffers. */
+	if (compositor->dmabuf_feedback_format_table &&
+	    version >= ZWP_LINUX_DMABUF_V1_MODIFIER_SINCE_VERSION) {
+		struct weston_dmabuf_feedback_format_table *table =
+			compositor->dmabuf_feedback_format_table;
+		unsigned int first = table->renderer_formats_indices.size /
+				     sizeof(uint16_t);
+		unsigned int n = table->size / sizeof(*table->data);
+
+		for (i = first; i < n; i++)
+			zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_send_modifier(resource,
+							  table->data[i].format,
+							  table->data[i].modifier >> 32,
+							  table->data[i].modifier & 0xFFFFFFFF);
+	}
 }
 
 /** Advertise linux_dmabuf support
